# Wordroom — environment
#
# Copy to apps/web/.env.local for local development, and set the same two values
# in the Vercel project. Both are public: `NEXT_PUBLIC_` is inlined into the
# browser bundle, and the anon key is meant to be. Its authority comes entirely
# from Row Level Security, which is why every table in supabase/migrations has a
# policy and why `answer` has no column grant.
#
# NEVER put SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY in this file or in apps/web. It bypasses
# RLS. The Edge Functions get it injected by the platform; nothing else needs it.

# Project URL, e.g. https://abcdefghijklm.supabase.co
# Locally, `supabase start` prints http://127.0.0.1:54321
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# The anon / publishable key. `supabase status` prints it locally.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase project settings this app depends on (dashboard, not env vars)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. Authentication > Providers > Anonymous sign-ins: ENABLED.
#    Every screen needs a bearer token before the player has typed anything.
#
# 2. Authentication > Providers > Google: ENABLED, if the sign-in nudge is to
#    offer it.
#
# 3. Authentication > Manual linking: ENABLED.
#    `linkIdentity` is how an anonymous player keeps their room and their locked
#    name when they sign in. Without it that call returns 422 and the only
#    alternative — signing in with Google instead — would create a second user
#    and strand the seat.
#
# 4. Authentication > URL Configuration > Redirect URLs: add
#    http://localhost:3900/auth/callback and the deployed
#    https://<domain>/auth/callback.
